  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nx4 + y4 + x2y2 = 21\n\nx2 + y2 - xy = 7 .....(1)\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nx4 + y4 + x2y2 = (x2 + y2 + xy) (x2 + y2 - xy)\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nx4 + y4 + x2y2 = 21\n\n⇒ (x2 + y2 + xy) (x2 + y2 - xy) = 21\n\n⇒ (x2 + y2 + xy) × 7 = 21\n\n⇒ (x2 + y2 + xy) = 21/7\n\n⇒ (x2 + y2 + xy) = 3 .....(2)\n\nSubtracting (2) from (1),\n\n- 2xy = 4\n\n⇒ xy = - 2\n\n⇒ (xy)² = 4\n\nPut xy = - 2 in equation (1),\n\nx2 + y2 = 7 - 2 = 5\n\nSo, (1/x²) + (1/y²) = (x2 + y2)/(xy)2 = 5/4\n\n**∴ The value of (1/x2) + (1/y2) is 5/4**",
